    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The handler is `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java:175-246`).\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Framework validation (before the handler body runs)\n\nThe body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto` with `@Valid` on the generated `OwnersApi` interface, so Bean Validation runs first:\n\n1. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n2. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$)`, `@Size(1..30)`\n3. **title** \u2014 `@Size(max 10)`\n4. **address** \u2014 `@Size(1..255)`\n5. **addressLine1 / addressLine2** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` each\n6. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n7. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern(^[-0-9 ().+]*$)`, `@Size(1..20)`\n8. **email** \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (note: **no** `@Email` format check here)\n9. **registrationDate / birthDate** \u2014 `@Valid` (cascade)\n\nThe `Owner` entity's own constraints (`@NotEmpty` on address/city/telephone, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone, `@NotEmpty` on first/last name in `Person`) are **declarative only** \u2014 nothing calls a `Validator` on the entity and `save` is not `@Valid`, so they are not enforced on this path.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Handler body, in execution order\n\n10. **Idempotency short-circuit** (178-187) \u2014 if the `Idempotency-Key` header was seen before and its owner still exists, return that owner with `200 OK` and stop (no create).\n11. **Address normalization** (191-197) \u2014 `normalizeAddress` on line1/line2/flat address (uppercase, collapse whitespace, expand ST/RD/AVE); composes a structured address if line1 present, else uses the flat address.\n12. **Required-field checks** (188-203) \u2014 `requireNonBlank` on firstName, lastName, composed address, city, telephone; accumulates into `missingFields` and throws `MissingRequiredFieldsException` if any are blank.\n13. **validatePostcode** (204) \u2014 optional; 4-digit format + region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099) \u2192 `InvalidFieldValueException`.\n14. **validateRegistrationDate** (205) \u2014 rejects a future date \u2192 `InvalidFieldValueException`.\n15. **Registration-date defaulting + business-day roll** (206-208) \u2014 defaults to `LocalDate.now()`, then `toBusinessDay` rolls weekends/public holidays forward.\n16. **requireDailyLimitNotReached** (209) \u2014 \u2265100 owners on that registration date \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException`.\n17. **requireCityBelowCapacity** (210) \u2014 \u226550 owners in the city \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException`.\n18. **Telephone normalization** (211-212) \u2014 `normalizeTelephone` \u2192 E.164 (`InvalidFieldValueException` on failure); written back onto the DTO.\n19. **Email normalization** (213-215) \u2014 if email present: trim, syntax-check via `EMAIL_PATTERN`, lowercase, reject disposable domains (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail) \u2192 `InvalidFieldValueException`.\n20. **Map DTO \u2192 entity** (218) \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwner` (MapStruct; ignores id and pets).\n21. **Set derived/normalized entity fields** (219-226):\n    - `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` (normalized)\n    - `registrationDate` (rolled value)\n    - `memberId` = `buildMemberId` (region + fiscal year + SHA-256(tel+lastName) + Luhn check digit, de-duplicated against existing member IDs)\n    - `namesakeCount` = count of case-insensitive first+last name matches\n    - `householdId` = SHA-256(version tag + normalized lastName + postcode)\n22. **requireUniqueIdentity** (227) \u2014 identity key = SHA-256(tel|email|soundex(lastName)); if any non-deleted owner matches \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (409).\n23. **markPossibleDuplicate** (228) \u2014 sets `possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf` if a same-postcode/same-soundex-lastName owner with a different identity exists (skipped when `sharesHousehold` is true).\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Persist and side-effects\n\n24. **Persist** (229) \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save(owner)` (thin pass-through, not `@Transactional`; id assigned here).\n25. **Record idempotency key** (230-232) \u2014 store `key \u2192 owner.id` in an in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap`.\n26. **Build response DTO** (233) \u2014 `toOwnerDtoWithBulkWarning`: sets bulk-signup warning, capacity warning, membership points/level (household-capped), and risk flag.\n27. **Audit log** (234-236) \u2014 `AUDIT` line with id/memberId/registrationDate/membershipLevel.\n28. **Construct + serialize OwnerCreatedEvent** (238-240) \u2014 increments `OWNER_CREATED_SEQUENCE` and writes the JSON to the `AUDIT` logger. **Not** published to any Spring listener \u2014 log-only.\n29. **Notify log** (241-242) \u2014 `NOTIFY` \"Welcome notification enqueued\" line. Log-only; no real email/queue.\n30. **Location header + response** (243-245) \u2014 `Location: /api/owners/{id}`, `201 CREATED`.\n\n**Notable gaps:** no password encoding (owners have none), no auto-timestamp beyond the explicit `registrationDate`, no JPA lifecycle hooks/entity listeners, and no real event bus or email \u2014 the \"event\" and \"notification\" are purely log statements."
